# HopOn Netherlands

## Run locally (Windows PowerShell)

Terminal 1, from the repository root:

```powershell
.\.tools\run-backend.ps1
```

This starts the Java 27 / Spring Boot API at `http://localhost:8080` using the Gradle 9.8.2 wrapper.

Terminal 2:

```powershell
cd frontend
npm ci
npm start
```

Use a Node.js version matching `^22.22.3 || ^24.15.0 || ^26.0.0` from `frontend/package.json`. Open `http://localhost:4200`. Angular proxies `/api/**` to the backend; `npm run start:lan` serves the UI on the local network.

The backend uses in-memory H2, so its data resets when it stops.

HopOn is an Angular mobile-first guide to Dutch cities. The current foundation includes the responsive app shell and Spring health endpoint.
